WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.503
NIST Special Publication 800-171 provides security requirements for protecting CUI in

00:00:05.503 --> 00:00:07.455
nonfederal systems and organizations.

00:00:07.455 --> 00:00:11.480
It is the principal technical and operational foundation for CMMC Level 2.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:17.320
The CMMC Level 2 model maps to 110 requirements from NIST SP 800-171 Revision 2.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.530
These requirements are organized across fourteen families covering areas such as access

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:22.405
control,

00:00:22.405 --> 00:00:26.655
awareness, audit, configuration, incident response, maintenance, and risk assessment.

00:00:26.655 --> 00:00:30.415
Other families address identification and authentication, media protection,

00:00:30.415 --> 00:00:34.640
personnel security, physical protection, security assessment, communications protection,

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.435
and system and information integrity.

00:00:36.435 --> 00:00:38.430
The requirements describe security outcomes,

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.890
but implementation depends on the organization's environment.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.500
Architecture, technology, workforce, contracts, data flows,

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.000
and operational constraints all shape how a requirement is satisfied.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.220
CMMC does not turn the NIST requirements into a product checklist.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:55.470
Assessors evaluate whether applicable practices are implemented within scope and supported

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.090
by objective evidence from policy,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.375
procedure, configuration, records, interviews, and observation.

00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:03.950
A System Security Plan describes the covered environment and how requirements are

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:04.720
implemented.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.935
Plans of Action and Milestones may have a limited role under program rules,

00:01:07.935 --> 00:01:12.340
but they are not a substitute for understanding current status and completing required

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.435
remediation.

00:01:13.435 --> 00:01:16.600
Organizations also need to monitor official transition guidance because standards and

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.240
contract requirements evolve.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.450
The applicable contract and current CMMC program materials determine which version and

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.520
assessment expectations govern a particular obligation.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.340
The key relationship is simple:

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.480
NIST SP 800-171 defines the Level 2 security requirement foundation,

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.275
while CMMC adds program structure for assessment, affirmation, status,

00:01:35.275 --> 00:01:37.000
and contractual verification.
